      Probes SBI extensions (TIME, IPI, RFNC, SRST) but does NOT probe or invoke any PMP-related SBI calls. This is architecturally correct: PMP is an M-mode construct managed by firmware (OpenSBI), and the SBI specification does not define standard PMP query/configuration calls for S-mode. The kernel's lack of PMP visibility is by design. The risk lies not in this function but in callers (machdep.c) that make PMP-related assumptions without being able to verify them.


